## Lore

The Ancient Master is a truly different character, and might be a little awkward
for an inexperienced player. This is an old man who devoted his entire youth to
the martial arts and to physical perfection, and has spent the last several
decades in a Tibetan monastery or a similarly remote retreat, mastering the
combat arts to the exclusion of all else. He has taught many others and led a
happy, fulfilled life.

It is time to see the world. The character has ventured beyond the austere walls
that were his home for so many years to explore a modern world that seems as
deadly and chaotic as the stories he has heard. As a disciple of discipline and
order he has decided that his place is here, in the eye of the storm, to bring
peace and harmony to the chaos-ravaged world. As a champion of order and light
you could expect nothing else.

## GM Notes

**The attributes have floors, not bonuses.** If the physical attributes come out
low even after physical skills are chosen, raise them to P.S. 18, P.P. 18 and
P.E. 20. Speed stays where it is. A low I.Q. is fine - wisdom and intelligence
are often strangers.

**Two dozen weapons are available but not carried.** Every mission may want a
different set, or none at all. Other personal items are minimal: no car, a
modestly furnished small apartment, simple clothes.

**Age and appearance** are rolled on printed 154-155. The age table starts at
40 on 01-16 and 50 on 17-33.
', 'published', 'data-script'
